course: dictionary
lesson: 13125
title: Fluttering: movement and feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your mind. Fluttering is one of them: it shows something moving lightly and quickly, up and down or to and fro. «The butterfly's fluttering wings caught the sunlight.» Picture small, quick wings. That is what fluttering means.
explain: Fluttering can also describe a feeling. «I had a fluttering feeling in my tummy before the school play.» You do not have real butterflies. The words around it tell you it is a light, nervous feeling, because the sentence is about a school play.
explain: Fluttering can describe a heart too. «Her heart was fluttering as she opened the letter.» A fluttering heart beats fast and unevenly. The clue is the letter: something exciting or scary is happening.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The flag was fluttering in the breeze» still makes sense if you say «the flag was moving quickly in the breeze», so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: Fluttering means moving quickly and lightly up and down or to and fro.
fact: Butterflies, moths, flags and falling leaves can all be fluttering.
fact: A fluttering feeling, like butterflies in your tummy, is a light nervous feeling.
fact: A fluttering heart beats fast and unevenly.
fact: Phrases to know: «fluttering wings», «fluttering in the breeze», «a fluttering in my tummy».
exercise: «The leaves were fluttering down from the trees.» What does fluttering mean here? | Loud and crashing | Burning brightly | Frozen completely still | *Moving quickly and lightly as they fall
exercise: «Mia had a fluttering feeling in her tummy before the school play.» What kind of feeling is this? | A hungry feeling | A feeling of great anger | *A light, nervous feeling | A sleepy feeling
exercise: «The flag was fluttering in the breeze, and the birds sang.» Find and copy the word that shows movement in this sentence. | *fluttering | birds | sang | breeze
test: «His heart was fluttering as he walked on to the stage.» What does a fluttering heart do? | *Beats fast and unevenly | Gets smaller each minute | Stops completely | Sings a song
test: Which phrase shows something moving lightly in the wind? | sweet and sour | *fluttering in the breeze | very cold and heavy | silent as a stone
exam: Eva says «the fluttering curtains» means the curtains are still and quiet. Is she right? | No, fluttering means a kind of food | Yes, fluttering means perfectly still | Yes, fluttering means very heavy | *No, fluttering means moving quickly and lightly
